# .aeg/packages — the static collision-domain list.
#
# Named as canonical by three governance docs that never had a file to point
# at: `.vinaya/projects.md` ("Routing vs. conflicts"),
# `aeg-root/iterations/README.md` §5, and `aeg-root/aeg-manual-flow.md` §init.
# This file is that missing artifact.
#
# WHAT A LINE MEANS. One collision domain per line: a repo-relative path
# prefix. Two tasks conflict if they touch the same domain (README §5) — the
# domains are declared and static; there is no dynamic path-overlap scanner
# (forbidden, §9/§10).
#
# WHO READS IT. `checkBlastRadiusScope` (packages/aeg-core/src/issue-validation.ts),
# wired into the `open-issue.ts` gate: a task Issue whose rationale names a path
# under a domain that no declared `Project:` owns must either list a second
# project or carry an explicit `blast-radius-ack:` line. The Planner also reads
# it by hand when declaring `conflicts-with` edges.
#
# DERIVATION, NOT INVENTION. Every `packages/*` workspace is a shared
# collision domain by construction (CLAUDE.md: "Shared infrastructure lives in
# packages"). The non-package entries below are the cross-cutting paths
# projects.md and README §5 both name verbatim — lockfiles, migrations, codegen
# output, monorepo config — which couple tasks *across* package boundaries.
#
# A domain being listed here does NOT by itself mean cross-product reach: a
# domain that is also a registered project's own path (e.g. `packages/aeg-core`
# is project `aeg-core`) is owned by that project, and a task declaring it is
# not under-declaring anything. Ownership resolves against `projects.md`.

